  "editorial_note": "GitHub listed only nine projects this Monday morning, and five of them were featured here in the past week. Today's four picks are two first appearances, ==MuJoCo after its 4.0 release== and Anthropic's Claude API quickstarts, and two earlier picks that have materially changed: Anthropic's skills repository, whose ==Office document skills moved to Apache 2.0== on 6 November, and OpenMausBot, which has shipped sixteen releases since we covered it on 30 October. Curation order reflects practical interest, not GitHub rank. Trending is not a release date or an endorsement.",
  "coverage_notes": [
    "GitHub's daily listing held only 9 rows at capture, fewer than on any day of the past week (13 to 18). The raw page was checked: it contains exactly nine listing rows, so the short list is GitHub's, not a parsing gap.",
    "All 9 listing entries were inspected. Exact public GitHub API metadata and recent releases were checked at about 07:02 UTC for the four picks and for vercel-labs/agent-browser; README files of the four picks were read at about 07:02:30 UTC; the anthropics/skills commit history since 31 October, the changed LICENSE.txt files before and after commit 2c5958e, and each skill folder's LICENSE.txt were read at about 07:04 UTC. Every checked repository was active and unarchived.",
    "Five entries featured in the past seven days were left out: sherlock-project/sherlock, dsx-ai-factory/nvke, meta/astryx and ranxianglei/billion-context (all picked yesterday, 8 November) and vercel-labs/agent-browser (6 November; latest release still v0.41.2 of 3 November).",
    "Two picks are repeats outside the seven-day window, each for a primary-sourced change: anthropics/skills (first picked 31 October) for its 6 November licence change, and milind-soni/OpenMausBot (first picked 30 October) for releases v0.1.135 to v0.1.150, including a meeting-notes bot in v0.1.147.",
    "The preceding seven calendar dates, 2-8 November, were checked for local history; all seven editions exist.",
    "The official listing was captured at 08:01:38 Europe/Paris. Literal stars-today labels are GitHub's displayed period figures; API total stars and README evidence were checked separately at the times shown per card. They are not an independently audited rolling 24-hour growth measurement.",
    "Feature descriptions come from each project's own README and release notes and are the maintainers' claims. No candidate code, installer, binary, plugin, skill or model was installed, downloaded or run, and none of this is a security audit or endorsement."
  ],
