      ],
      "description": "MuJoCo (Multi-Joint dynamics with Contact) is Google DeepMind's ==general-purpose physics engine for robotics, biomechanics and machine learning==. It has a C API, Python bindings and a Unity plug-in, and simulates articulated bodies touching their environment.",
      "why_interesting": "Version 4.0.0 shipped on 6 November. Its release notes list ==speculative contacts that stop fast objects tunnelling through thin walls==, elasto-plastic springs and deformable bodies that keep a permanent bend, and a split of the Python package into mujoco-core, mujoco-studio and the default mujoco.",
      "caveat": "4.0 is a major version with ==several breaking changes==: new tendon side-site semantics, the cable plugin and composite element removed, Python 3.10 support dropped. The release notes warn that upgrading the pip package in place needs an uninstall or forced reinstall first."
    },
