      ],
      "description": "Anthropic's public collection of ==Agent Skills: folders of instructions, scripts and resources== that Claude loads for a task, plus the Agent Skills specification and a template. It holds 19 skills, from design and testing to the docx, pdf, pptx and xlsx document skills.",
      "why_interesting": "This is a repeat with a material change. When we first covered it on 31 October, the four document skills were source-available under Anthropic's terms only. Commit 2c5958e, merged on 6 November, ==moved docx, pdf, pptx and xlsx to Apache 2.0==, so the most complex production skills here can now be studied and reused like the rest.",
      "caveat": "GitHub still detects no repository-wide licence: each skill carries its own LICENSE.txt, and ==doc-coauthoring has none==. The README calls the skills demonstration and educational material whose behaviour may differ from Claude's. Skills include scripts an agent runs, so review them like code."
    },
