      "description": "A desktop chat app for macOS, Windows and Ubuntu where ==each AI bot is a contact with its own model, computer and connected apps==. Bots run on the claude, codex or grok command-line tools already signed in on your machine.",
      "why_interesting": "A repeat with material change: since our 30 October pick it has published sixteen releases, v0.1.135 to v0.1.150. Version 0.1.147 added ==a notes bot that joins Google Meet, Teams or Jitsi calls== as a guest and posts a summary, decisions and transcript; others added parallel threads per bot, team sharing and several workspaces.",
      "caveat": "A meeting bot records other people, so ==participants' consent is needed==. Outside a MausBot Cloud plan, transcription needs your own ElevenLabs, Groq or OpenAI key, or a local Whisper model. Cloud computers come from the paid third-party Boat service after a trial, and near-daily releases mean frequent change."
    },
