      "description": "Anthropic's ==starter projects for building on the Claude API==: a customer-support agent, a financial data analyst, computer-use and browser-use demos, minimal browser and computer toolset drivers, an autonomous coding agent, and a growing set of Managed Agents examples for Slack, Linear, Sentry and more.",
      "why_interesting": "It shows working patterns rather than snippets. The newest Managed Agents examples include a ==Sentry autofix agent that reproduces a bug with a failing test== and opens a pull request for human review, with credentials kept outside its sandbox and a hard spend cap, and a knowledge wiki rebuilt on 6 November.",
      "caveat": "Every quickstart ==needs a Claude API key and paid usage==. The README says the toolset examples are not production code, and the macOS computer-use reference controls a real desktop, which it advises running in a VM."
